# Cloudflare Pages security headers.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file only takes effect at the ROOT of the deployed bundle.
# The homepage folder is rsynced to the bundle root by deploy-isaac-site.sh, so
# it lands at /_headers and applies site-wide (homepage + /portfolio/ + extras).
# A copy under /portfolio/_headers is IGNORED by Cloudflare Pages.
#
# CSP is deliberately omitted: the site relies on inline scripts, external CDN
# libraries (three.js, etc.) and loads arbitrary user files in the preview pane
# — a strict CSP would break those, so we apply the safe subset instead.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# NOTE: you CANNOT shorten the asset TTL from here. Cloudflare Pages serves
# /portfolio/app.js with `public, max-age=14400` and OVERRIDES the max-age in
# this file — a `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` rule only
# gets `must-revalidate` merged into the Pages default (verified 2026-10-08).
# The stale-bundle fix is therefore the content-hash cache-bust token that
# deploy-isaac-site.sh rewrites into /portfolio/index.html (`app.js?v=<hash>`).
